ent :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388308}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "935951a4-ee2a-54bc-9e42-14a72505ef8e" :question/math-academy-id "q-133968" :question/problem "A teacher wants to determine whether a student's performance in mathematics influences their performance in physics. The following table shows the grades of $5$ students in a mathematics and physics class. \n\n| **Math Grade** | **$8$** | **$6$** | **$8$** | **$4$** | **$5$** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **Physics Grade** | $9$ | $5$ | $8$ | $4$ | $3$ |\n\nWhich of the following scatter plots represents this data?" :question/worked-solution "We create a scatter diagram in the coordinate plane as follows:\n\n- First, we draw the independent variable (math grade) along the horizontal axis.\n\n- Then, we draw the dependent variable (physics grade) along the vertical axis.\n\n- Finally, we plot the points that correspond to the pairs from the data.\n\nThis gives us the following scatter plot.\n\n![](images/5b/5bdbaadf2d3ea794c145365f5ee61ee4c1551dc72b62c8a681933b9aac74d214.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186388314 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152233 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "79f1049a-8af9-50ee-9dac-9dbd9c19bdc6" :knowledge-point/title "Correctly Identifying a Scatter Plot"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1d96ca6e-aa39-56b6-a603-08fb5fae2a80" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/72/726a22a7d72af2ba9a7b9c9568cc1723557ee8c0af4dd38a3dd9bacca4f72769.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388316} {:answer/id #uuid "9816374b-f222-57ec-9346-41bf02f900e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/ef/ef920634ab0391c8b13566e8575ee66839bcaf38dd6e4d87bfa336035ab10166.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388317} {:answer/id #uuid "66b02031-af4a-5dc1-ac7f-ed1163e286f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/b7/b741264e080009d9e634e7ffce5e9041b6cd65b34e4d840700397a7378255ea8.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388318} {:answer/id #uuid "448502eb-fb15-5ab2-9d96-04aeaf2da0b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/8e/8ea63450225d8b50e6f00e012afcd3afe8215eb573ed3a31ce9aa57c30ec8132.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388319} {:answer/id #uuid "8388f37e-7b04-57a4-a21b-751817dec11b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/81/81364754556cfeed2c4a2b74d2c745c054491e7f0a9e1d2512fffe6dc4569e5d.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388320}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "66b02031-af4a-5dc1-ac7f-ed1163e286f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/b7/b741264e080009d9e634e7ffce5e9041b6cd65b34e4d840700397a7378255ea8.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388318} :answer-field/id #uuid "da2b298a-e144-5d4b-ab37-e427ce14674c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388315}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "711b7d57-8e73-5262-a6cb-c7a387e51978" :question/math-academy-id "q-133969" :question/problem "Lucy, who plays basketball, notices that the number of points she scores in a game increases as a function of the number of hours she practices her jump shot each week. She records the following data.\n\n| **Number of Hours Training** | **$4$** | **$6$** | **$7$** | **$8$** | **$10$** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **Points Scored per Game** | $8$ | $12$ | $16$ | $20$ | $28$ |\n\nWhich of the following scatter plots represents this data?" :question/worked-solution "We create a scatter diagram in the coordinate plane as follows:\n\n- First, we draw the independent variable (number of hours training) along the horizontal axis.\n\n- Then, we draw the dependent variable (points scored per game) along the vertical axis.\n\n- Finally, we plot the points that correspond to the pairs from the data.\n\nThis gives us the following scatter plot.\n\n![](images/b7/b741264e080009d9e634e7ffce5e9041b6cd65b34e4d840700397a7378255ea8.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186268961 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152235 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7f99f2aa-f977-5d6e-ae62-a826a897ba9b" :knowledge-point/title "Reading a Scatter Plot"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "93b0f7b8-b781-54c4-a185-a692da720e33" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "90%" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267467} {:answer/id #uuid "93c6b873-1244-55dd-a5d0-7e953959f130" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "85%" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267468} {:answer/id #uuid "ba35ff19-d85c-5142-84b2-93a8f390294b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "70%" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267815} {:answer/id #uuid "ce9bdb9f-cdf1-552b-86b5-3b68d3b691fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "75%" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267992} {:answer/id #uuid "da1adb01-9156-561a-b4db-38e2dc065dd9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "80%" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268075}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "93c6b873-1244-55dd-a5d0-7e953959f130" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "85%" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267468} :answer-field/id #uuid "0c7565e4-dc8a-5b42-b83a-83fc7e504012" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268431}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "43fcfab7-3240-5e37-8741-3769fb9bd3d5" :question/math-academy-id "q-134043" :question/problem "![](images/80/80d08441967f6c1a4026fe9ca0d2bdfdde8fac57a2ae0a7b8d6b34889f3469bd.png)\n\nThe scatter plot above shows the relationship between hours of study per week and the overall percentage obtained by students in a math class. What was the overall percentage obtained by the student who studied, on average,  $7$ hours each week?" :question/worked-solution "![](images/39/39e7370f9cf517a7a139fecf71561041a9b1470150e0fa333d3fff679f77882d.png)\n\n    \n\nTo determine the overall percentage obtained by the student who studied $7$ hours each week, we locate $7$ on the horizontal axis and move in the vertical direction until we find some points, as shown above.\n\nThe highlighted point has coordinates $(7,85).$ Therefore, the student who studied $7$ hours each week obtained an overall percentage of $85%.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186398382 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152235 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7f99f2aa-f977-5d6e-ae62-a826a897ba9b" :knowledge-point/title "Reading a Scatter Plot"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3b931d3b-ada2-5b04-a7ba-3e5388b9aa35" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398384} {:answer/id #uuid "ce0bbf2c-bd3b-5933-b107-38c36abe9e06" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398385} {:answer/id #uuid "1275d8d1-87ea-51ac-80ba-d13b5b0d06d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398386} {:answer/id #uuid "c0d3ff95-8a16-5335-b1eb-84d2fbc5830f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398387} {:answer/id #uuid "cf078eaa-4e8e-529e-aeaf-cf7c18b72b3c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398388}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1275d8d1-87ea-51ac-80ba-d13b5b0d06d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398386} :answer-field/id #uuid "c816f258-3ddf-536d-ab66-8610e4b22204" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398383}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6b5dde64-1d37-5f32-890c-5a590a1188e6" :question/math-academy-id "q-134085" :question/problem "![](images/55/551ed1182231e19a08653c86ffb7b117c2dc9497b6927f6287ffcd10651b5f56.png)\n\nThe scatter plot above shows the relationship between the number of absences in a month and the size of a class. How many absences were there in a class whose size is $20$ students?" :question/worked-solution "![](images/80/8088e41a66b4aba259d95f3099f71d5777caf876e9278e6b7f11c865ab12f7e0.png)\n\nTo determine the number of absences there were in a class whose size is $20$ students, we locate $20$ on the horizontal axis and move in the vertical direction until we find some points, as shown above.\n\nThe highlighted point has coordinates $(20,6).$ Therefore, there was a total of $6$ absences in the month for the class with $20$ students."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186269103 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083306 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a75b47ec-8d5a-545e-b915-daca92320322" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Non-Roots of a Polynomial Using the Rational Roots Theorem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1482f361-3b1e-543f-870b-a26dcf92d2ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266319} {:answer/id #uuid "2870d2f6-a4e4-5d62-a218-0e3e5a8a8827" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266504} {:answer/id #uuid "447ea00c-4d69-5351-8ae6-7fb524a5e59a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266757} {:answer/id #uuid "ab240971-126a-51ed-95e8-caf2152e97e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267690} {:answer/id #uuid "fda09780-5082-5dc7-9e43-74a04e529440" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268378}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "447ea00c-4d69-5351-8ae6-7fb524a5e59a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266757} :answer-field/id #uuid "466acc84-20e7-58f4-bf70-73eea0fa85ba" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268526}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "54404730-020a-547b-8cd2-8751476ed4d0" :question/math-academy-id "q-13613" :question/problem "According to the rational roots theorem, which of the following **cannot** be a root of the polynomial $f(x)=3{x}^{3}+10{x}^{2}-23x+10?$" :question/worked-solution "Given a polynomial with integer coefficients, the rational roots theorem states that any rational roots of the polynomial must take the form\n\n$$\n\\pm \\frac{\\text{factor of the constant term}}{\\text{factor of the leading coefficient}}.\n$$\n\nFor the given polynomial $f(x),$ the constant term is $10$ and the leading coefficient is $3.$ So, any rational roots of $f(x)$ must take the form\n\n$$\n\\pm \\frac{\\text{factor of }10}{\\text{factor of }3}.\n$$\n\nOf the given answer choices, only $3$ does not take the above form. The value $3$ can be interpreted as a fraction $\\frac{3}{1},$ and the numerator $(3)$ is not a factor of $10.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176347 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176058 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "66a1733a-d7bb-5c86-a154-9e54422053a7" :knowledge-point/title "Utilizing the Oddness Property of the Tangent Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "19df7d47-b87b-5e46-8360-7533c525ec2c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266358} {:answer/id #uuid "3c2908b8-2ead-5a77-be9f-804bc07bb7fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266672} {:answer/id #uuid "6ccc1b1b-9a04-5bb8-a591-9f5cc4c7efc6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267102} {:answer/id #uuid "8b14d04b-7661-55d9-a6d2-74ec1e93a05a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267392} {:answer/id #uuid "a5bfc5ef-972c-5d0d-9011-6abdfdf11b45" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267642}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "19df7d47-b87b-5e46-8360-7533c525ec2c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266358} :answer-field/id #uuid "a6737d96-a059-592e-9cfb-df4b5f79acd2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268703}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ccd7ae50-1c4e-5bcc-8b8b-d405f5154f0b" :question/math-academy-id "q-136548" :question/problem "If $tan⁡a=-2,$ then $tan⁡(-a)=$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the graph of $y=tan⁡x.$\n\n![](images/df/df1aba3f5ff980de82a74dde8170ad708e379caf2188873bcddc83177e87c7a6.png)\n\nOur graph has rotational symmetry of order $2$ about the origin. If we rotate the graph ${180}^{∘}$ around the origin, we get the same picture. This means that $tan⁡x$ is an *odd* function, and we have\n\n$$\ntan⁡(-x)=-tan⁡x.\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}tan⁡(-a) & =-tan⁡a \\\\  & =-(-2) \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186269128 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176059 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d4b378b0-30e5-59a8-b9f7-882b5e226a2e" :knowledge-point/title "Utilizing the Evenness Property of the Secant Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "04ba9a98-d418-5054-94e5-129c6b76bfac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266186} {:answer/id #uuid "19edb75b-03b9-59e8-bc8e-e9f768d59cb2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266360} {:answer/id #uuid "5e2ed2c4-f432-5dc5-84ad-45be5e6c0e95" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266975} {:answer/id #uuid "5e32262d-72d6-5e5a-894e-153eb250705f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266977} {:answer/id #uuid "f0b9b848-8717-52db-b148-c872c7061d08" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268284}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "04ba9a98-d418-5054-94e5-129c6b76bfac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266186} :answer-field/id #uuid "aa7bd88