-{7}^{x}+3?$" :question/worked-solution "To plot the given function, we follow these steps:\n\n- We take the curve $y={7}^{x}.$\n\n![](images/28/283470740585f9ddba5e81ccf2c2fcb7d34d339ab26cb0ea35aae2bac4b85e1b.png)\n\n- Reflect it on the $x$-axis to give $y=-{7}^{x}.$ The $y$-intercept moves from $(0,1)$ to $(0,-1)$ but the horizontal asymptote stays at $y=0.$\n\n![](images/66/66a1dd2866d56323de98e2ec0bf665ebb20d7d770cbd8691a825749d660f125d.png)\n\n- Then, vertically shift it by $3$ units up to give $y=-{7}^{x}+3.$ The point $(0,-1)$ moves to $(0,2)$ and the horizontal asymptote moves from $y=0$ to $y=3.$\n\n![](images/7a/7a1b3b562e4489b8b649f20d3133960dda7e5213827adb2bf7fd94e6659a64c4.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186390666 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115369 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "623f4440-ba1a-58ce-9ff2-ccdf591a0d30" :knowledge-point/title "Vertical Reflections of Exponential Decay Functions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "22b59601-a89e-5e1d-a669-b2b7a7e8029b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/50/50a0caebc732fec06957fadef2326f89cfef7f94d278e2ecc2774ad5168c0374.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390668} {:answer/id #uuid "f12c77ec-9cb6-5bae-a7a4-e6c90735d0ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/c6/c653557a459c6fd4989737d418e22e642aeed4e03193ea08c8d55dd43ca9ede8.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390669} {:answer/id #uuid "492d6d67-62e0-56d1-8a29-7869d43f0e28" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/ef/efbb630d38c907b1ce053bd5fa9a14b305d4392b4b573cd294348f7360d2d327.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390670} {:answer/id #uuid "5d556352-d259-5a3a-b309-08f3051bd6ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/56/56ed5bc3bf1dd167086f6057a7c39b070055c375b9d8c9e316ac987fca404a98.png" :db/id